{"term":"dentist","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9b66c1f56b130319d2","definition":"A medical doctor who specializes in teeth.","example":"It is singular how forcibly this passage in my narrative brings to my mind a picture which used to be, some years ago, at a broker's—that charnel-house of the comforts and graces of life. It had been taken out of its frame, and leant in a dark and dusty corner against a perpendicular armchair, whose rigid uprightness seemed suited only to the parlour of a dentist, repose being the last idea it suggested.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["10th dentist","dentistess","dentist gold","dentistic","dentistical","dentistlike","dentistress","dentistry","nondentist","surgeon-dentist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dentist#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3439ee2b715d51c268","definition":"Deliberate misspelling of Dengist.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet, alt-of, deliberate, misspelling","register":"Internet, alt-of, deliberate, misspelling","wordFamily":["10th dentist","dentistess","dentist gold","dentistic","dentistical","dentistlike","dentistress","dentistry","nondentist","surgeon-dentist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dentist#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈdɛntɪst/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a4/En-us-dentist.ogg/En-us-dentist.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["10th dentist","dentistess","dentist gold","dentistic","dentistical","dentistlike","dentistress","dentistry","nondentist","surgeon-dentist"]}